  "summary": "The released 1.1.0 portable app includes run-bound anomaly triage: inspect channel episodes with explicit recovery, gap, context and censored boundaries, add human notes, and download the review tied to its originating run.",
  "rationale": "The original label-isolated detector and metrics remain unchanged. An actual extracted-app analyst journey verifies a known spike, annotation export and note reset between analyses; independently restoring the previous version field reproduced every old benchmark hash before version-only IDs were refreshed. This makes the downloadable workflow match the practical source feature without claiming operational anomaly assurance.",
  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic telemetry and bounded rule-based detector evidence; no live spacecraft or hardware validation.",
    "Human notes are detached local downloads rather than server-persisted multi-user reviews.",
    "Unsigned desktop portable folders, not system installers or clean-machine proof. Three-OS extracted-native checks drive an owned URL; default OS browser opening remains manual."
  ],
